  {"clause_id": "c067", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The assignment is made \"without any warranty whatsoever\" and disclaims all title warranties, yet the next paragraph assigns \"any and all rights and privileges possessed by\" Assignor under its deeds and leases. Whether that grant carries any implied assurance of what Assignor in fact possesses is contestable.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c068", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The indemnity covers claims \"incident to, or arising directly or indirectly from, operations by Assignee\" with no express mention of Assignor's own negligence or fault. It also overlaps Section 8(A) of the Farmout Agreement without saying which governs post-assignment operations.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c069", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The rights assigned are those \"necessary or convenient\" for operation, maintenance, reworking and production, a standard with no boundary — \"convenient\" in particular could reach far beyond the well. The grant is then made \"expressly subject to\" the underlying leases without identifying them.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.17}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c070", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The form reserves an overriding royalty at a blank rate on a blank substance and contains no escalation mechanism, while Section 4 fixes 12.50% of 8/8 with reserved rights to escalate to 16% and 18.75% (and 1.5%/3.5%/6.5% for burdened oil) on Payout. The executed assignment and Section 4 cannot both state the royalty regime.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c071", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"[G]rants, conveys and assigns other such rights to Assignee only to the extent set forth herein\" is garbled — \"other such rights\" has no antecedent — while the same sentence reserves title to \"the aforementioned lands, and all rights connected thereto.\" What passes to Assignee is left to inference.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c072", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This paragraph permits Assignee to assign on written notice provided it retains at least a 25% working interest, while Section 15(D) of the Farmout Agreement forbids any assignment by Farmee without Farmor's prior written consent. The two consent regimes are irreconcilable on their face.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c073", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The reservation of all strata \"extending below the ___ formation\" leaves the formation name blank, so the vertical limit of the grant is measured by nothing, while Section 3(E) measures depths earned as 100' below total depth drilled and not more than 4,000'. Which limit controls the assigned depths cannot be determined.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c074", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The assignment is made binding on and for the benefit of \"their respective successors and assigns,\" which is in tension with the restriction in the same instrument (and Section 15(D)) barring assignment without Assignor's consent. Whether a non-consented successor takes the benefit is unaddressed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c075", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The assignment is made \"subject to the terms and conditions of that certain unrecorded Farmout Agreement,\" so the recorded conveyance's extent depends on an unrecorded instrument, and Section 17 says the Farmout's covenants \"run with said Farmout Lands.\" How the Farmout's terms bind third parties or survive its Section 13 termination is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
  ]}
]}

